abstract: >-
  GRUS-STD-60084 v2.0-U is a jurisdiction-neutral measurement
  standard specifying how resource consumption by large
  computational loads is measured and reported from the filed
  record: a two-axis facility classification (workload shape
  W-1/W-2/W-3; cooling type C-1 through C-5), boundary water
  quantities derived from first principles, five evidence grades,
  and a ten-step reproducible measurement protocol. Published
  free for adoption by any jurisdiction. Texas edition of record:
  Public Utility Commission of Texas Project No. 58317, Item 96.
  Also filed: Ohio PUCO Case No. 24-0508-EL-ATA; Arizona
  Corporation Commission Docket No. E-01773A-26-0123.
